     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily is **6,000 mg/day**, well above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day (many hospitals cap at 3,000 mg/day). Even with normal liver function, that dose carries a significant risk of hepatotoxicity. Also, a single 2000 mg dose is above the standard maximum of 1,000 mg.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **1000 mg PO every 8 hours** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4,000 mg/day, the max)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you intended 2000 mg per dose, or a total above 4 g/day, for a specific reason, let me know. Pharmacy and the order system will likely flag it anyway, so you may need to follow your institution's override process.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency, plus any details like PRN versus scheduled, indication, or duration, and I'll prepare the order."
     }
