      "type": "text",
      "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming the dose doesn't change the risk: 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is well above the maximum daily dose and could cause serious liver injury in this patient, even with normal liver function. I'm not able to put through an order I believe could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range**, such as 1000 mg PO q8h (3 g/day) or 1000 mg PO q6h (4 g/day).\n- **Draft a note to pharmacy** if you're aiming for a specific therapeutic effect, so they can suggest alternatives such as scheduled acetaminophen plus another analgesic class.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If the target is better pain or fever control, I can help you build a multimodal regimen.\n\nIf you believe there's a clinical rationale for exceeding the limit, that decision should go through your institution's pharmacy review and override process, not through me. Which of these would you like?"
     }
